 "solutions": [
  {
   "question": "1",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Let $f(x)=e^{3x^2}$. Then $f'(x)=6x\\,e^{3x^2}$. Answer C.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "2",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\tan(2x-1)=2\\sec^2(2x-1)$. Answer D.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "3",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Method 1: $f'(x)=\\dfrac{\\sec^2 x}{\\tan x}=\\dfrac{1}{\\cos^2 x}\\div\\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}=\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x\\sin x}=\\sec x\\,\\text{cosec}\\,x$.\n\nMethod 2: $f(x)=\\ln(\\sin x)-\\ln(\\cos x)$, so $f'(x)=\\dfrac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}+\\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}=\\dfrac{\\cos^2x+\\sin^2x}{\\sin x\\cos x}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x\\cos x}$. Answer C.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "4",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Largest value is $77$ and smallest is $30+x$, so $77-(30+x)=43$, giving $x=4$. From the calculator, the sample standard deviation is $13.14904696\\ldots\\approx 13.15$. Answer B.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "5",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Data A has a strong negative correlation and Data B has no correlation. Answer D.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "6",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Categorical data is non-numerical; ordinal data can be placed in a reasonable order (first, second, third, \\ldots). Answer C.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "7",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Cumulative percentage at cricket is $54\\%$ and at swimming is $30\\%$, so cricket is $54\\%-30\\%=24\\%$. Answer B.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "8",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int 4e^{8x}\\,dx=\\dfrac{4e^{8x}}{8}+C=\\dfrac{1}{2}e^{8x}+C$. Answer A.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "9",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int(4x+3)^6\\,dx=\\dfrac{1}{28}(4x+3)^7+C$. Answer D.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "10",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$y=\\displaystyle\\int\\left(3-2x^{-2}\\right)dx=3x+\\dfrac{2}{x}+c$. When $x=1,\\ y=-2$: $3+2+c=-2$, so $c=-7$. Answer D.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "11",
   "part": "a",
   "latex": "Frequency $=220-130=90$.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "11",
   "part": "b",
   "latex": "\\exfigure{629_q11_s1}",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "11",
   "part": "c",
   "latex": "Half of $300$ is $150$; reading across to the ogive and down gives approximately $73$ km/h (about $72.5$).",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "12",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Total weight of 14 $=14\\times78.9=1104.6$ kg.\n\nTotal weight of 15 $=15\\times(78.9+1.03)=1198.95$ kg.\n\n$\\therefore$ the 15th person's weight is $1198.95-1104.6=94.35$ kg.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "13",
   "part": "a",
   "latex": "From the calculator, $r=0.9476628\\ldots$ This is a strong positive correlation.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "13",
   "part": "b",
   "latex": "From the calculator, $A=-1.236979\\ldots$ and $B=0.85329\\ldots$, so the equation is $y=0.85x-1.24$ (2 d.p.).",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "14",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Ordered 2020 scores: $10, 16, 18, 20, 22, 27, 30, 32, 33, 34, 34, 35, 38$ (13 scores). $Q_1=19,\\ Q_2=30,\\ Q_3=34$; minimum $10$, maximum $38$.\n\n\\exfigure{629_q14_s1}\n\nSkewness: 2019 is a symmetrical distribution; 2020 is negatively skewed (stronger performance).\n\nLocation: 2019 median $=23$; 2020 median $=30$, which is significantly higher (better performance).\n\nSpread: 2019 range $=26$, IQR $=14$; 2020 range $=28$, IQR $=15$; the classes were consistent in the gap between their poorer and stronger results.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "15",
   "part": "a",
   "latex": "The school may be concerned because students have the right to keep their own scores private, since it is their personal data. One way to address this concern would be to supply the scores without names or classes attached, making the data anonymous and only useful in aggregate.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "15",
   "part": "b",
   "latex": "\\exfigure{629_q15_s1}",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "15",
   "part": "c",
   "latex": "The line of best fit estimates an English score of approximately $59$. This is not a valid estimate as there are numerous outliers in the top right of the graph representing students who are high achievers in both subjects.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "15",
   "part": "d",
   "latex": "The moderate negative correlation indicates that students tend to do more poorly in English when they excel in Mathematics, and vice versa. This suggests that most students split their time and effort between these subjects, and investing more in one subject means investing less in the other.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "15",
   "part": "e",
   "latex": "This line cannot be used to predict scores in other schools as there are too many influencing factors that differ from one school context to the next, which may lead their data to look completely different and not be accurately represented by this model.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "16(a)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}e^{5x}=5e^{5x}$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "16(b)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{4x}{2x^2}=\\dfrac{2}{x}$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "16(c)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Let $u=e^{3x}+4$, so $u'=3e^{3x}$, and $v=x^3$, so $v'=3x^2$.\n\n$$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{vu'-uv'}{v^2}=\\dfrac{x^3(3e^{3x})-(e^{3x}+4)(3x^2)}{x^6}=\\dfrac{3x^2\\left(xe^{3x}-e^{3x}-4\\right)}{x^6}=\\dfrac{3\\left(xe^{3x}-e^{3x}-4\\right)}{x^4}$$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "16(d)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=3\\times4\\cos^3x\\times(-\\sin x)=-12\\sin x\\cos^3x$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "16(e)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "With $u=x^2$, $u'=2x$, $v=e^{12x}$, $v'=12e^{12x}$:\n\n$f'(x)=4\\left(vu'+uv'\\right)=4\\left[e^{12x}(2x)+x^2(12e^{12x})\\right]=4e^{12x}(2x+12x^2)=8xe^{12x}(1+6x)$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "16(f)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$f'(x)=\\cos x-2\\sin 2x$, so $f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)=\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}-2\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}-2\\times\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "17(a)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$m^3-4m^2+m+C$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "17(b)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int(4y^3)^{\\frac12}dy=\\int2y^{\\frac32}dy=\\dfrac{2y^{\\frac52}}{\\frac52}+C=\\dfrac{4y^{\\frac52}}{5}+C=\\dfrac45\\sqrt{y^5}+C$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "17(c)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "Since $\\dfrac{d}{dx}a^x=a^x\\ln a$, $\\displaystyle\\int a^x\\,dx=\\dfrac{a^x}{\\ln a}+c$.\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int6^{2x}dx=\\dfrac12\\int2\\times6^{2x}dx=\\dfrac12\\times\\dfrac{6^{2x}}{\\ln6}+C=\\dfrac{6^{2x}}{2\\ln6}+C$.\n\nA primitive function is $\\dfrac{6^{2x}}{2\\ln6}$ (i.e. $C=0$).",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "17(d)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int\\left(3x^2-x+\\dfrac2x\\right)dx=x^3-\\dfrac{x^2}{2}+2\\ln|x|+C$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "17(e)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "If $f(x)=3x^3+10x^2$ then $f'(x)=9x^2+20x$. So\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int(45x^2+100x)(3x^3+10x^2)^3dx=5\\int(9x^2+20x)(3x^3+10x^2)^3dx=\\dfrac54(3x^3+10x^2)^4+C$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "17(f)",
   "part": null,
   "latex": "$\\dfrac{dV}{dt}=4\\pi\\left(\\dfrac14t\\right)^2=\\dfrac{\\pi t^2}{4}$, so $V=\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{\\pi t^2}{4}dt=\\dfrac{\\pi t^3}{12}+C$.\n\nInitially deflated: $t=0,\\ V=0$, so $C=0$ and $V=\\dfrac{\\pi t^3}{12}$.\n\nWhen $t=6$, $V=\\dfrac{\\pi\\times6^3}{12}=18\\pi$. The volume of gas is $18\\pi\\ \\text{cm}^3$.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "17(g)",
   "part": "a",
   "latex": "$\\text{RHS}=\\dfrac{2}{x+4}+\\dfrac{2x+10}{x^2+10x+24}=\\dfrac{2(x+6)}{(x+4)(x+6)}+\\dfrac{2x+10}{(x+4)(x+6)}=\\dfrac{2x+12+2x+10}{(x+4)(x+6)}=\\dfrac{4x+22}{(x+4)(x+6)}$ as required.",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  },
  {
   "question": "17(g)",
   "part": "b",
   "latex": "$\\displaystyle\\int\\left(\\dfrac{2}{x+4}+\\dfrac{2x+10}{x^2+10x+24}\\right)dx=2\\ln|x+4|+\\ln|x^2+10x+24|+C$",
   "marks_breakdown": null,
   "source": "extracted"
  }
